# From the tests of the first compiler: src/lexer.rs, `hexadecimal_and_binary_numbers`.
==== 1
---- file a.azl (no newline at end)
0x
---- run lex a.azl
---- exit 1
---- stdout (empty)
---- stderr
error[E0105]: a hexadecimal number is `0x` followed by the digits 0-9 and a-f, as in `0x1F`
 --> a.azl:1:1
  |
1 | 0x
  | ^
---- asserted 1:1 a hexadecimal number is `0x` followed by the digits 0-9 and a-f, as in `0x1F`
==== 2
---- file a.azl (no newline at end)
0b
---- run lex a.azl
---- exit 1
---- stdout (empty)
---- stderr
error[E0105]: a binary number is `0b` followed by the digits 0 and 1, as in `0b1010`
 --> a.azl:1:1
  |
1 | 0b
  | ^
---- asserted 1:1 a binary number is `0b` followed by the digits 0 and 1, as in `0b1010`
